i_video: add touch controls

With BADGE_PANEL_TOUCH=1, fingers drive panel_touch.h, and its output
reaches the game as the events a joystick, a mouse and a keyboard would
send: the stick moves, the look area turns, the buttons fire, use, change
weapon and open the menu, and in the menu the stick and buttons are the
arrow and select keys. The controls are drawn over each frame, and a
close request quits at once. The window has no minimum size, so on an
output smaller than the frame the frame is scaled down to fit rather
than cut off. Without the variable nothing changes.

